  "result": "Shell completion now treats `#` as an ordinary character, so arguments like `a#b` or `#c` complete correctly. The tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment and drops everything after it. For example, completing `cli a#b` lost the rest of the word.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so nothing is treated as a comment.\n\nI added a regression test, `test_split_arg_string_hash`, which checks that `\"cli a#b #c\"` splits into `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"#c\"]`. I did not add a `CHANGES.md` entry.",
